  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@mill413/dsh-notify",
      "text": "English | [中文说明](README.zh.md)\n\nDesktop notifications and configurable HTTP pushes for DeepSeek Harness. Get a reminder when a task stops running or needs approval, an answer, or plan review. Clicking a desktop notification returns you to its session.\n\nThe published version is **0.4.2**, validated with npm **DSH 0.2.1-rc.3**. Other host versions have not been verified. MIT licensed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "The plugin is published on npm; no source build is needed:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add @mill413/dsh-notify@0.4.2\n```\n\nUse the DSH CLI that runs your target profile, with the same `DSH_HOME`. If you use Launcher, use its configured `DSH_LAUNCHER_DSH_COMMAND`. The package includes its bundle patch; do not edit the host or profile manually."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Reload DSH and refresh the page after installation. On installations managed by `dsh-web.service`, restart that user service once installation is complete, then check its status."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notification channels",
      "text": "| Channel | Events | Requirements |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Desktop notification | Main session stops running; new approval, question, or plan-review request | Keep the DSH page open and allow browser notifications |\n| HTTP push | Main agent changes from running to idle; an agent requests approval or asks a question | Keep the DSH host running; the browser may be closed |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Notification channels",
      "text": "Subagent completion does not produce a separate completion alert; subagent approval and question requests do. Desktop notifications are sent only while the page is hidden or unfocused by default. This restriction does not apply to HTTP pushes.\n\n“Task complete” refers to a running-to-idle transition and does not guarantee success. The HTTP channel does not subscribe to a separate plan-review event. Initial browser snapshots establish a baseline and do not replay old alerts."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "1. Open **Plugins → Desktop notifications (dsh-notify)** and expand its settings.\n2. Grant browser notification permission, then send a test notification.\n3. Choose completion, attention-needed and background-only preferences, then save.\n4. For HTTP delivery, configure your endpoint and request, test it, then enable and save."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "Desktop notifications and HTTP pushes have separate master switches. Completion and attention-needed preferences are shared between the channels. The HTTP test uses the current unsaved form and works while the channel is disabled."
    },
    {
      "section": "HTTP configuration",
      "text": "Requests run on the DSH host. An endpoint containing `localhost` refers to that machine. Supported methods are `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH` and `GET`; GET has no body. You may configure authentication headers, a body template and an icon URL. Endpoint URLs must use HTTP(S) and cannot contain a username or password.\n\nDefault body:\n\n```json\n{\"title\":\"{{title}}\",\"body\":\"{{body}}\",\"level\":\"{{level}}\",\"group\":\"{{group}}\",\"icon\":\"{{icon}}\"}\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "HTTP configuration",
      "text": "Template variables: `title` (session title), `body` (event summary), `event` (`complete`, `approval`, `question`, or `test`), `level`, `group`, `sessionId`, `time` and `icon`. Unknown variables are left unchanged. Substitution applies to body values, not URLs, headers or JSON keys. Valid JSON is parsed before substitution and serialized afterwards; other bodies are treated as text without URL encoding."
    },
    {
      "section": "HTTP configuration",
      "text": "A request with a body defaults to `application/json` unless a Content-Type header is supplied. Requests time out after five seconds. There is no retry or offline queue; HTTP 2xx is treated as successful delivery to the configured endpoint, not proof of delivery to a recipient."
    },
    {
      "section": "Privacy and troubleshooting",
      "text": "HTTP delivery is disabled by default and has no built-in third-party destination. Only the endpoint you configure receives requests. The default template sends the session title and event summary; the plugin does not proactively send conversation contents. Credentials are stored with the plugin settings in the DSH profile and are not encrypted by this plugin. Do not commit real request headers or credential-bearing screenshots."
    },
    {
      "section": "Privacy and troubleshooting",
      "text": "The test route uses DSH authentication. Users with access to it can ask the host to contact a configured HTTP address, including addresses on its network. Follow the host's access controls."
    },
    {
      "section": "Privacy and troubleshooting",
      "text": "- Desktop notifications require HTTPS or a browser-recognized secure local context, browser permission, and an open page. Check system Do Not Disturb and the background-only setting if no alert appears.\n- This plugin uses the Notification constructor without a Service Worker. Some mobile browsers do not support it. Use HTTP delivery when the browser will be closed.\n- For HTTP failures, verify network reachability, request headers and receiver logs from the host machine, then use **Test push**."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Use Node.js 22.18.0 or newer and the package manager declared in `package.json`. SDK development dependencies come from npm and are pinned to the target DSH version; the repository does not depend on an adjacent Harness checkout.\n\n```sh\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm run verify\npnpm run test:release\npnpm test"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "The package includes host code, browser UI, locale files, its bundle patch and icon. The settings UI supports Chinese and English; default HTTP titles and bodies are Chinese and can be customized through the body template. See [publishing instructions](docs/publishing.md) for the GitHub/npm release workflow."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE) © 2026 mill413."
    }
  ],
